# Prettier must never touch Markdown in this repository.
#
# Prettier's Markdown printer is not configurable in the ways that matter: it
# pads every table cell to the widest cell in its column, rewrites list
# markers, and renumbers ordered lists. Several docs tables have a wide
# free-text column -- the widest row in docs/docs/logging.md is 815 characters
# -- so prettier turns a readable table into rows of that width and produces an
# unreadable diff on every save. There is no option to disable this.
#
# This matters even though prettier is not part of the documented workflow:
# Zed bundles prettier and will format Markdown on an explicit Format command
# with no setup at all.
#
# Honoured by the prettier CLI, the VS Code Prettier extension, Zed's built-in
# prettier, and conform.nvim -- including when prettier is invoked via
# --stdin-filepath, where it passes content through unchanged and exits 0.
#
# Markdown structure is enforced by markdownlint instead; see
# .markdownlint-cli2.yaml.
*.md
